  {
   "id": "4wdlXrLvIAAJ",
   "from": "Ross Gayler",
   "author": "8757f45da80a9e6c",
   "date": "2016-06-20T05:42:57Z",
   "subject": "dplyr::mutate seems unexpectedly slow",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>I have been using dplyr to data wrangle a modestly large tbl_df (~2.4 million rows by ~80 columns) on my not particularly fast laptop. Most operations are pleasantly fast, but some are surprisingly (to me) slow).<br><br>In the code below, the <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">arrange() %&gt;% group_by()</span> takes ~20 seconds, whereas the relatively trivial <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">mutate()</span> takes ~20 minutes.<br><br>There are ~600k groups, each of ~4 rows .<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">last_file_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input_files$as_at_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This is quite slow (~20 minutes). The mutate() is unexpectedly slow.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>d </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&lt;&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ungroup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  arrange_</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> id</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> as_at_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># order rows by as-at date within entity</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  group_by_</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> id</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># check each entity</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  mutate_</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    first_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> first</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">as_at_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># first observed as-at date for this entity</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    last_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">last</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">as_at_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># last observed as-at date for this entity</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    last_date_ok </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> last_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> last_file_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    n_dates </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    is_consecutive </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">as_at_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> first_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">as_at_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lag</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">as_at_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> months</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    all_consecutive </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> all</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">is_consecutive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><b>Does anyone have any suggestions as to why the <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">mutate()</span> is comparatively slow? </b><br><br>The only thought that has occurred to me is that there is a significant overhead per group overhead in mutate and here I have very many tiny groups. If that is the case, there is probably nothing I can do to speed it up without constructing artificially larger groups and simulating the effect of smaller groups in the mutate logic, which would remove the clarity of the code.<br><br>Thanks<br><br>Ross<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "y0lc3RcLIQAJ",
   "from": "Hadley Wickham",
   "author": "b756a7daa2c2aa6d",
   "date": "2016-06-20T14:04:59Z",
   "subject": "Re: dplyr::mutate seems unexpectedly slow",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Can you try creating each new column in it&#39;s own mutate? That would\r<br>help narrow down if there&#39;s a function that&#39;s particularly slow, or\r<br>it&#39;s just overhead related to the many groups.\r<br>\r<br>Hadley\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Mon, Jun 20, 2016 at 12:42 AM, Ross Gayler &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">r.ga...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I have been using dplyr to data wrangle a modestly large tbl_df (~2.4\r<br>&gt; million rows by ~80 columns) on my not particularly fast laptop. Most\r<br>&gt; operations are pleasantly fast, but some are surprisingly (to me) slow).\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; In the code below, the arrange() %&gt;% group_by() takes ~20 seconds, whereas\r<br>&gt; the relatively trivial mutate() takes ~20 minutes.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; There are ~600k groups, each of ~4 rows .\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; last_file_date &lt;- max(input_files$as_at_date)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; # This is quite slow (~20 minutes). The mutate() is unexpectedly slow.\r<br>&gt; d %&lt;&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   ungroup() %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   arrange_(~ id, ~ as_at_date) %&gt;% # order rows by as-at date within entity\r<br>&gt;   group_by_(~ id) %&gt;% # check each entity\r<br>&gt;   mutate_(\r<br>&gt;     first_date = ~ first(as_at_date), # first observed as-at date for this\r<br>&gt; entity\r<br>&gt;     last_date = ~ last(as_at_date), # last observed as-at date for this\r<br>&gt; entity\r<br>&gt;     last_date_ok = ~ last_date == last_file_date,\r<br>&gt;     n_dates = ~ n(),\r<br>&gt;     is_consecutive = ~ (as_at_date == first_date) |\r<br>&gt;       (as_at_date == (lag(as_at_date) + months(6))),\r<br>&gt;     all_consecutive = ~ all(is_consecutive)\r<br>&gt;   )\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Does anyone have any suggestions as to why the mutate() is comparatively\r<br>&gt; slow?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; The only thought that has occurred to me is that there is a significant\r<br>&gt; overhead per group overhead in mutate and here I have very many tiny groups.\r<br>&gt; If that is the case, there is probably nothing I can do to speed it up\r<br>&gt; without constructing artificially larger groups and simulating the effect of\r<br>&gt; smaller groups in the mutate logic, which would remove the clarity of the\r<br>&gt; code.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Thanks\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Ross\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; --\r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups\r<br>&gt; &quot;manipulatr&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an\r<br>&gt; email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">manipulatr+...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">manip...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; Visit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/manipulatr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/manipulatr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357183940000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1OtYQR43wpi-MTzdgb4bY8\">https://groups.google.com/group/manipulatr</a>.\r<br>&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357183940000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1WMwQBPbsr0pKFPIxyuZZi\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br><a href=\"http://hadley.nz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://hadley.nz&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357183940000&amp;usg=AOvVaw26KuxDiSZf7SD5RpPH1trw\">http://hadley.nz</a>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
